From 1287c2b7cfffe52dfd9e789fd483ff33b49adee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH 5/8] wifi: mt76: do not dereference a NULL chandef when

 setting a channel

__mt76_set_channel() dereferences phy->chandef.chan when deciding
whether to reset dfs_state, without checking that a channel was ever
assigned. phy->chandef is only assigned from a channel context, and none
of those assignments runs before mt76_phy_init(), so a phy that has
never been assigned one has a NULL chan here.

That state is reachable: mt76_scan_work() is queued on every phy in
dev->scan.phy_mask, and that mask is built from the requested channels,
so a scan covering both bands runs scan_work on the phy of the band that
never had an interface. scan.c also restores with
mt76_set_channel(phy, &phy->main_chandef, false), passing a NULL
destination.

Drop a transition to no channel, which is not a channel change, and
treat an unknown current channel as an unknown dfs state. Returning
early also keeps phy->chan_state non-NULL for mt76_update_survey() and
mt76_get_survey().

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
 mac80211.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1061,6 +1061,15 @@ int __mt76_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	int timeout = HZ / 5;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* A phy without an operating channel cannot be switched to one.
+	 * mt76_phy_init() does not set chandef, it is only assigned from a
+	 * channel context, so a phy that has never been assigned one has a
+	 * NULL chan here. Dropping the transition keeps chan_state valid
+	 * for mt76_update_survey() and mt76_get_survey() below.
+	 */
+	if (!chandef->chan)
+		return 0;
+
 	mt76_worker_disable(&dev->tx_worker);
 	mt76_txq_schedule_pending(phy);
 
@@ -1068,7 +1077,8 @@ int __mt76_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	wait_event_timeout(dev->tx_wait, !mt76_has_tx_pending(phy), timeout);
 	mt76_update_survey(phy);
 
-	if (phy->chandef.chan->center_freq != chandef->chan->center_freq ||
+	if (!phy->chandef.chan ||
+	    phy->chandef.chan->center_freq != chandef->chan->center_freq ||
 	    phy->chandef.width != chandef->width)
 		phy->dfs_state = MT_DFS_STATE_UNKNOWN;
 
